      "is_best": true,
      "html": "<div class=\"post__content post__content--new-editor\"><p>Welcome ​<user-mention data-id=\"106359\">@TyrantRenre</user-mention>, to the community!</p><p>You can find this information on the <a href=\"https://www.st.com/en/evaluation-tools/steval-ipmm15b.html\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">product website of the STEVAL-IPMM15B</a>, for example, in <a href=\"https://www.st.com/resource/en/user_manual/um2704-1500-w-motor-control-power-board-based-on-stib1560dm2tl-sllimm-2nd-series-mosfet-ipm-stmicroelectronics.pdf\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">UM2704</a>, fig. 17, or by taking a look at the <a href=\"https://www.st.com/resource/en/board_manufacturing_specification/steval-ipmm15b_gerber.zip\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">GERBER data</a>. Since the connector has a notch to prevent reverse polarity, the corresponding 34-pin plug on a ribbon cable usually fits.</p><p>Hope that answers your question?</p><p>Regards<br/>/Peter</p></div>"
